Built stdlib-only compress.py with both requested CLI modes, mixed-radix encoding for structured text, and a bzip2 fallback for other input. The 44,267-byte corpus compresses to 16,833 bytes—a 61.9739% reduction, beating default zlib’s 22,390 bytes. Verified byte-identical restoration through the CLI and 15 additional edge-case round trips; the registered assay reports 61.9739 with zero spread across three runs.